WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:17.368 --> 01:19.537
Ah! Hello.

01:20.038 --> 01:21.164
Welcome!

01:23.541 --> 01:25.502
-You look beautiful.
-Give me a hand.

01:25.585 --> 01:26.419
Here we go.

01:26.503 --> 01:27.879
-Let me get it.
-Help me with this.

01:27.962 --> 01:28.797
Okay.

01:37.597 --> 01:38.431
Smile.

01:38.515 --> 01:39.516
YALASHANG FILM CLUB

01:40.141 --> 01:41.893
One, two, three.

01:43.353 --> 01:44.479
I'll take one more.

01:45.522 --> 01:46.815
Okay, smile.

01:48.733 --> 01:50.610
One, two, three.

01:53.655 --> 01:56.199
If I say I can't
go tomorrow, what do I mean by that?

01:56.282 --> 01:59.160
Tonight is our last night. You get it?

02:00.745 --> 02:02.789
Yeong-beom, it's our last night.

02:05.792 --> 02:09.045
I swear I'm going to, damn it.
What's wrong with you?

02:34.529 --> 02:36.656
How do I know? I don't know what I want,

02:36.739 --> 02:40.618
and you don't know until
you walk down the aisle with someone.

02:41.286 --> 02:44.914
Just watch, okay?
I'm going to see you in a wedding dress.

02:45.456 --> 02:46.708
Ta-da!

02:47.208 --> 02:48.751
They're pretty.

02:49.252 --> 02:50.170
Wow.

02:55.508 --> 02:57.218
Okay. This is tricky.

03:00.597 --> 03:02.223
See? I told you I'd see it.

03:02.307 --> 03:04.434
Oh? Hey, over here.

03:04.517 --> 03:06.060
Hey!

03:06.686 --> 03:09.939
My heart was pounding
for all the new people in my life,

03:10.023 --> 03:11.733
as well as the old.

03:12.859 --> 03:13.818
Whoo!

03:13.902 --> 03:14.986
Ooh!

03:16.070 --> 03:17.071
Wow.

03:17.155 --> 03:19.157
It was an accident, I swear.

03:20.450 --> 03:22.911
I felt like
I could fly up to the clouds,

03:22.994 --> 03:24.454
just like those balloons.

03:27.749 --> 03:30.001
SUCH AN UNEVEN LOVE

03:35.465 --> 03:38.259
There was someone new
in Mom's world as well.

03:39.552 --> 03:42.430
A plump little human
had come into her life.

03:42.931 --> 03:46.517
HAPPY FIRST BIRTHDAY
FROM YEOM BYEONG-CHEOL, NA MIN-OK

04:04.244 --> 04:08.122
Though this was
their son's child, for some reason,

04:09.582 --> 04:12.085
they felt even greater affection for him.

04:12.752 --> 04:15.630
Don't babysit too often,
no matter how cute they are.

04:16.172 --> 04:18.883
They only stay that way
if you don't get sick of them.

04:18.967 --> 04:22.512
Once Geum-myeong gets married,
you'll need to draw the line clearly.

04:22.595 --> 04:24.305
You two have your own lives.

04:26.349 --> 04:29.519
Everyone says he has my eyes,
but look at that piehole!

04:29.602 --> 04:31.896
-Just like his mom's!
-"Mouth," son. Mouth.

04:35.817 --> 04:38.778
I invited your family, too,
but they're not coming?

04:40.113 --> 04:41.030
Pretty much, yeah.

04:41.572 --> 04:44.200
I also wouldn't visit
my unemployed son-in-law.

04:46.494 --> 04:48.329
I thought maybe your brothers?

04:50.081 --> 04:50.915
They said

04:51.958 --> 04:53.626
they never wanna see our asses again.

04:55.211 --> 04:56.254
Faces.

04:56.754 --> 04:57.630
Sorry?

04:58.256 --> 04:59.507
Our "faces."

05:02.969 --> 05:05.346
-Who's faces?
-Your faces.

05:07.557 --> 05:08.933
Right. Our faces.

05:13.271 --> 05:15.481
That's 19 grams of pure gold.

05:15.565 --> 05:19.068
They must've said "19 grams"
about a dozen times over the phone.

05:19.152 --> 05:20.611
It's for his college tuition.

05:21.237 --> 05:23.823
He's a stingy one, isn't he?

05:23.906 --> 05:27.535
If he wants to pay for tuition,
he should consider inflation.

05:27.618 --> 05:28.828
They have the money.

05:29.996 --> 05:32.290
All that rice-cake money,
and this is all they bought?

05:32.373 --> 05:33.249
Yeah.

05:33.333 --> 05:35.126
I heard that Grandpa sports
a Mercedes-Benz.

05:35.209 --> 05:38.087
Of course he does.
Everyone eats rice cakes, after all.

05:42.050 --> 05:43.718
This isn't very classy of them.

05:44.218 --> 05:46.095
What? Like you are?

05:48.181 --> 05:50.224
Mm-mm, let's go.

05:50.308 --> 05:53.061
Ooh, okay, okay. Mm.

05:53.144 --> 05:55.063
YANG CHE-IL'S FIRST BIRTHDAY

05:55.563 --> 05:57.607
Are you sure you can afford
that stuff right now?

06:00.651 --> 06:02.695
I'm gonna do everything on his birthdays.

06:02.779 --> 06:04.655
Not like you guys ever
did anything for mine.

06:04.739 --> 06:05.823
Listen, it was a tough time.

06:05.907 --> 06:08.451
Sure. Times always got tough
right around my birthday.

06:08.534 --> 06:11.037
So how do you plan
to support this new family?

06:11.871 --> 06:13.122
Will you mooch off us?

06:13.206 --> 06:14.957
-I have business ideas.
-Of course.

06:15.541 --> 06:16.459
With Cheol-yong?

06:16.542 --> 06:18.294
You better not still mean
that pawn shop, son.

06:18.378 --> 06:20.129
Well, Pops, you only live once, so--

06:20.213 --> 06:21.881
Oh, I'm happy to smack you twice.

06:22.715 --> 06:24.801
People are supposed to mature
when they have a child.

06:24.884 --> 06:27.011
-Why can't you grow up?
-I'd never expect help from you.

06:27.095 --> 06:29.764
Look, Eun-myeong,
we're not asking for the impossible.

06:29.847 --> 06:33.434
You just have to get up early, all right?
Head on down to the loading docks.

06:33.518 --> 06:35.853
They have plenty of jobs there.

06:37.230 --> 06:40.358
So I can live a life like yours?
Is that what this is about?

06:41.401 --> 06:42.276
Look, Dad,

06:42.360 --> 06:45.738
if you wanna fill a bucket up with water,
you must turn the nozzle on all the way.

06:45.822 --> 06:48.783
If you waste all your time
patching the holes, it'll never get full.

06:49.367 --> 06:50.952
Don't you understand that?

06:51.035 --> 06:53.579
It's not just Geum-myeong.
I have dreams too.

06:53.663 --> 06:55.706
I don't want to be a dad
of a family of four

06:55.790 --> 06:58.709
who goes to a barbecue place
but only buys dinner for three.

06:58.793 --> 07:00.962
I'll be a dad
who gets as much as he wants.

07:22.900 --> 07:25.027
Do you have to talk to your dad like that?

07:25.945 --> 07:29.240
Our Steelheart is softer than you think.
You hurt his feelings.

07:32.160 --> 07:34.704
Then remind him of Geum-myeong
and cheer him up.

07:34.787 --> 07:35.830
You little…

07:36.998 --> 07:38.916
How do you get more bitter every year?

07:39.542 --> 07:42.003
I think you two should be thankful
I even made it this far.

07:42.086 --> 07:43.713
Kids feel it when parents believe in them.

07:43.796 --> 07:45.548
You put faith in Geum-myeong,
and she soared.

07:45.631 --> 07:46.466
Goodness.

07:46.549 --> 07:48.968
But both of you ignored me
and didn't support my goals.

07:49.051 --> 07:50.595
Unbelievable.

07:50.678 --> 07:53.806
Can you carry him for a while?
My arms are hurting.

07:56.517 --> 07:58.269
I'll take him.

07:58.352 --> 08:00.521
Give me Che-il, and you two can go inside.

08:00.605 --> 08:03.065
Give him to me. Aw, sweet baby.

08:04.775 --> 08:06.611
Oh my goodness.

08:23.127 --> 08:27.298
Never in a million years
did I think my daughter would do this.

08:27.798 --> 08:29.425
I've just been so upset.

08:29.509 --> 08:32.261
I feel like the sky has collapsed on me.

08:32.345 --> 08:33.763
It's my fault.

08:34.555 --> 08:36.724
I can't tell you how sorry I am.

08:38.184 --> 08:41.437
You can't even have a lead ring
if you get married pregnant,

08:41.521 --> 08:43.439
let alone a golden one.

08:44.357 --> 08:46.484
I never got to have my own wedding.

08:47.109 --> 08:50.029
Now my daughter
won't get to wear a veil either.

08:51.155 --> 08:55.785
I know it seems like Eun-myeong
is still struggling to find his way,

08:55.868 --> 08:57.620
but as a person, he's--

08:57.703 --> 08:58.663
It's not that.

08:59.163 --> 09:00.915
Eun-myeong isn't the problem.

09:02.250 --> 09:03.084
Really?

09:03.876 --> 09:06.963
Eventually, every son becomes his dad.

09:07.046 --> 09:08.714
I've always envied your life.

09:08.798 --> 09:11.342
I've envied your life
more than anyone else's.

09:13.219 --> 09:15.638
You're the one with a wealthy husband.

09:16.806 --> 09:18.307
Every field day,

09:19.350 --> 09:22.562
I had to drag my three kids with me
under the scorching sun.

09:23.396 --> 09:26.357
But one time,
I saw your husband fanning your back

09:26.440 --> 09:27.900
so you could cool off.

09:28.609 --> 09:30.319
Oh, come on now.

09:30.945 --> 09:32.905
Only you notice that kind of thing.

09:33.781 --> 09:34.949
It made me cry.

09:36.284 --> 09:39.954
I thought, "How is that woman
so blessed to have a man that devoted?"

09:41.038 --> 09:45.084
"And what sin did I commit
to deserve this pile of dog shit?"

09:48.212 --> 09:49.213
Anyway,

09:50.590 --> 09:51.882
is Hyeon-suk getting along?

09:52.883 --> 09:55.052
She doesn't know how to do anything.

09:55.553 --> 09:58.514
If she doesn't catch on,
feel free to yell at her.

09:58.598 --> 10:01.267
A good cry might teach a new mom a lesson.

10:01.350 --> 10:02.935
I won't yell at her.

10:03.019 --> 10:04.604
I won't make her cry,

10:05.313 --> 10:08.524
and I'll make sure
Hyeon-suk gets a nice ring too.

10:09.692 --> 10:11.319
She will.

10:12.361 --> 10:15.615
If you ever wanna see Hyeon-suk
or your first grandson,

10:17.325 --> 10:19.118
you just come on over.

10:19.201 --> 10:21.329
Or tell me to come out to see you.

10:21.829 --> 10:25.625
After all, we're in-laws now.
That counts too, Yeong-ran, doesn't it?

10:29.962 --> 10:32.965
How can he look exactly like my daughter?

10:37.720 --> 10:40.348
So you can't win
with your daughter either?

10:44.518 --> 10:47.063
One of
my mom's poems was called

10:48.272 --> 10:50.024
"My Damn Child."

10:50.107 --> 10:51.651
Come on! What's the big deal?

10:51.734 --> 10:53.653
Good grief.

10:53.736 --> 10:55.029
That's enough, you brat!

10:55.112 --> 10:57.365
-I've had it with you! Ooh. Ow!
-Stop.

10:57.448 --> 11:00.409
Is she saving the country?
Will the company fail without her?

11:00.993 --> 11:02.536
Uh-uh! Nope. Give it to me!

11:02.620 --> 11:03.746
Stop it!

11:03.829 --> 11:05.581
What is your son
supposed to do with liquor?

11:05.665 --> 11:07.833
Cheol-yong picked out a terrible present!

11:07.917 --> 11:10.086
It's because my parents make me miserable.

11:10.169 --> 11:12.546
So she's missing
her own nephew's birthday.

11:13.673 --> 11:15.800
Try to understand your sister, huh?

11:15.883 --> 11:18.636
She's having a rough time at work, okay?

11:19.220 --> 11:22.139
She thinks she's so great
'cause she works for a big corporation.

11:22.223 --> 11:23.933
Which of us will be here
to take care of you?

11:24.016 --> 11:25.601
Which of us will be here when you're old?

11:25.685 --> 11:28.187
We don't need you to take care of us.

11:28.270 --> 11:30.648
First, figure out
how to take care of yourself.

11:30.731 --> 11:33.192
…in South Korea,
is on the verge of bankruptcy.

11:33.275 --> 11:36.404
Don't be so harsh on him.
He might have to pick out your grave.

11:36.487 --> 11:40.282
…the largest of Korea's corporations
are immune from the shock.

11:40.366 --> 11:43.411
The effects of a Kia bankruptcy
would be felt throughout the economy.

11:43.494 --> 11:44.745
Kwon Jae-hong reports.

11:45.329 --> 11:48.374
This afternoon, Korea First Bank
announced at a press conference

11:48.457 --> 11:51.168
that of the 28 subsidiaries
under Kia Group,

11:51.252 --> 11:52.712
18 of them will be subject…

11:52.795 --> 11:55.881
It was a harvest season
when you reaped what you sowed,

11:55.965 --> 11:57.800
whether that was a golden toad

11:59.552 --> 12:01.095
or a postdated check.

12:49.268 --> 12:51.145
Stop the layoffs! Not one more!

12:51.228 --> 12:53.063
Stop the layoffs!
Not one more!

12:53.147 --> 12:55.024
We won't let you show us the door!

12:55.107 --> 12:56.901
We won't let you
show us the door!

12:56.984 --> 12:58.986
Stop the layoffs! Not one more!

12:59.069 --> 13:00.863
Stop the layoffs!
Not one more!

13:00.946 --> 13:02.448
We won't let you show us the door!

13:02.531 --> 13:05.826
Major corporations are
crumbling in the Asian financial crisis

13:05.910 --> 13:07.995
as unemployment continues to grow.

13:09.705 --> 13:12.792
An unforgettable winter
was on its way.

13:13.501 --> 13:16.378
The Dainong Group,
the 34th largest company in Korea,

13:16.462 --> 13:18.589
has effectively been dissolved.

13:18.672 --> 13:22.635
Of Dainong's four subsidiary companies,
only Midopa will be spared.

13:22.718 --> 13:24.470
The courts will oversee the sales of

13:24.553 --> 13:27.473
Dainong Heavy Industries Company
and Metro Product,

13:27.556 --> 13:29.767
both subsidiaries of the Dainong Group.

13:29.850 --> 13:32.436
Ssangbangwool Development
and Ssangbangwool Corporation

13:32.520 --> 13:34.647
have officially
been declared bankrupt today.

13:34.730 --> 13:37.316
Taeil Precision Company
is the latest high-profile firm

13:37.399 --> 13:39.819
to adopt bankruptcy prevention measures.

13:39.902 --> 13:44.365
Taeil Precision and its subsidiaries
carry a debt of 970 billion won.

13:44.448 --> 13:46.826
Chohung Bank
and other bond finance agencies…

13:46.909 --> 13:49.453
Stocks have plunged
again today, with the S&amp;P falling…

13:49.537 --> 13:53.582
First of all, thank you for giving me
the opportunity to speak with you today.

13:53.666 --> 13:56.460
…panic among investors.
With unemployment soaring, the economic…

13:56.544 --> 13:57.920
I wanted to thank you

13:58.003 --> 14:00.589
for letting me know
the results of the interview.

14:01.382 --> 14:03.759
Thank you so much
for giving me the opportunity.

14:03.843 --> 14:06.262
I am willing to do
whatever it takes to, uh…

14:07.304 --> 14:11.725
Willing to do whatever it takes
to join your organization. Allow me to…

14:11.809 --> 14:13.853
If you look at
the list of toothpaste products

14:13.936 --> 14:15.729
that were exported to Northeast Asia,

14:16.480 --> 14:20.150
this is a toothpaste that wasn't on
the list of imported toothpaste,

14:20.234 --> 14:22.820
and you won't be able
to find it even if you try.

14:23.445 --> 14:27.700
This toothpaste
will destroy common cavities,

14:28.701 --> 14:29.869
guaranteed,

14:30.452 --> 14:32.037
and whiten yellow teeth.

14:32.121 --> 14:35.833
This product is now in the hands of
a leading American toothpaste company

14:35.916 --> 14:38.168
recognized by the WHO

14:38.711 --> 14:41.630
following the bankruptcy of
its original manufacturing company.

14:42.131 --> 14:45.509
It's buy-one-get-one-free.
You won't hear a better offer.

14:45.593 --> 14:48.304
…has filed for bankruptcy
and finalized the process today.

14:48.387 --> 14:51.265
Ladies and gentlemen,
our government has made a request

14:51.348 --> 14:54.310
to the International Monetary Fund
to carry out its bailout plan.

14:54.393 --> 14:58.564
In spite of Korea's reputation as
an exemplary case of economic development,

14:58.647 --> 15:01.692
the government has been forced
to admit to national bankruptcy

15:01.775 --> 15:05.070
and is now pursuing means of recovery
from international organizations.

15:05.154 --> 15:07.323
The government
is now cautiously considering

15:07.406 --> 15:10.242
the timing of the application
and the scale of the aid…

15:10.326 --> 15:13.245
The next stop is Sillim Market,

15:13.329 --> 15:15.039
formerly Cannes Theater.

15:15.122 --> 15:16.832
…expected to be around 30 billion…

15:16.916 --> 15:19.877
The next stop is Sillim Market,

15:19.960 --> 15:21.962
formerly Cannes Theater.

15:42.066 --> 15:44.234
CANNES THEATER WILL SHUT DOWN
ON DECEMBER 1

15:44.318 --> 15:46.070
When one door closes,

15:48.072 --> 15:50.699
another door creaks open.

15:57.581 --> 15:59.708
TICKET, JA 17

16:09.760 --> 16:13.138
Come on, man.
Just take an empty seat.

16:19.186 --> 16:20.688
JA 17

16:23.190 --> 16:26.110
Excuse me.
Could you put your leg down?

16:26.694 --> 16:27.778
You heard the lady.

16:48.924 --> 16:50.426
Alfredo.

17:12.239 --> 17:13.991
They say
the stars have to align

17:14.074 --> 17:16.118
for you to meet someone
once in a lifetime.

17:16.201 --> 17:19.204
But to meet three times
is really pushing it.

17:24.209 --> 17:25.669
Hey, I saw her.

17:26.879 --> 17:27.713
Did you?

17:28.338 --> 17:29.882
-Huh?
-You missed her?

17:31.050 --> 17:32.801
This isn't the time
to be collecting trash.

17:32.885 --> 17:36.764
Life hands you a gift on a silver platter,
and you still kick it to the curb.

17:39.183 --> 17:41.351
If you
miss that third chance,

17:42.853 --> 17:44.813
you'll have to wait till the next life.

17:44.897 --> 17:45.814
Geum-myeong!

17:58.619 --> 18:01.080
Last time,
it was Seo Taiji playing.

18:01.705 --> 18:04.833
-This time, it was H.O.T.
-Geum-myeong! Geum-myeong!

18:11.590 --> 18:12.633
Oh, watch it!

18:33.695 --> 18:35.030
Geum-myeong! Wait!

19:04.768 --> 19:06.687
That's when he realized…

19:09.940 --> 19:11.775
you get only three chances,

19:11.859 --> 19:14.486
but if the clock runs out,
and it's still a tie-game,

19:15.612 --> 19:17.489
there's always the penalty shoot-out.

19:39.803 --> 19:40.804
Stop!

19:43.265 --> 19:44.099
Please, stop!

19:44.183 --> 19:45.601
When one door closes…

19:46.143 --> 19:49.229
-Please!
-…without fail, another door creaks open.

19:49.313 --> 19:50.647
You could've caught the next one.

19:50.731 --> 19:52.232
Jeez.

19:52.858 --> 19:53.859
Thank you.

20:12.586 --> 20:16.089
Had the 1997
financial crisis not happened…

20:19.343 --> 20:21.136
had I not lost my job…

20:26.183 --> 20:28.644
had the theater not been
going out of business…

20:35.400 --> 20:39.238
had any of these things not happened
exactly as they did…

20:46.286 --> 20:48.705
Everyone, off. Last stop.

20:49.331 --> 20:52.876
…perhaps this moment
would never have happened.

20:59.800 --> 21:01.093
Is this a dream?

21:03.262 --> 21:04.096
Am I dreaming?

21:05.722 --> 21:06.556
Yeah.

21:16.191 --> 21:18.527
I chased you down
all the way from the theater.

21:19.111 --> 21:20.487
I ran to catch this bus.

21:20.570 --> 21:22.364
I knew no matter what,

21:23.156 --> 21:24.825
I had to catch up with it.

21:28.537 --> 21:29.371
Were you

21:30.330 --> 21:31.415
at the theater alone?

21:32.791 --> 21:33.709
-Yes.
-I see.

21:37.838 --> 21:40.382
-And you… you were--
-Yeah, yeah.

21:44.094 --> 21:45.012
Wow.

21:46.305 --> 21:47.306
Finally.

21:48.098 --> 21:49.474
Yes, finally.

21:49.558 --> 21:53.061
I guess… this is when you use that word.

22:25.302 --> 22:27.012
Why do you keep laughing?

22:29.639 --> 22:33.060
Your style has really changed
since I last saw you.

22:33.143 --> 22:35.604
You're no longer like Picasso, aren't you?

22:35.687 --> 22:36.772
Oh, I still am.

22:36.855 --> 22:38.023
I'm an art instructor.

22:38.523 --> 22:40.525
Picasso Art Academy offered me a job.

22:41.234 --> 22:43.779
-Whoa!
-Without me, the academy would be doomed.

22:44.821 --> 22:46.990
-So they pay me well.
-Mm.

22:47.074 --> 22:50.285
I think that's, uh, that's amazing?

22:52.371 --> 22:53.372
Me too.

22:54.790 --> 22:55.999
I think it's amazing.

23:01.505 --> 23:04.674
The amazing thing is that
we were both at the theater.

23:04.758 --> 23:08.136
It sounds crazy, but I go every day
in the hopes you'd show up.

23:09.971 --> 23:11.890
Um, I've been thinking about you.

23:16.812 --> 23:17.854
I missed you a lot.

23:25.487 --> 23:26.947
I should go.

23:27.030 --> 23:28.073
N… now?

23:28.156 --> 23:30.283
Oh, unless it's too soon?

23:33.495 --> 23:34.871
Is it too soon?

23:37.332 --> 23:40.127
Uh, let's order something.

23:40.210 --> 23:41.461
Let's order beer. Yeah.

23:41.545 --> 23:44.548
Uh, beer? Sounds good.

23:45.173 --> 23:46.758
JINRO SOJU

23:51.596 --> 23:52.639
Hey.

23:53.974 --> 23:56.309
Why do you keep staring at me?

23:58.353 --> 23:59.938
You're driving me nuts.

24:00.021 --> 24:01.356
You're right.

24:02.023 --> 24:03.358
And as a matter of fact,

24:04.025 --> 24:05.193
I'm also going nuts.

24:06.611 --> 24:09.364
-Oh!
-I swear, this never happens.

24:09.448 --> 24:11.533
Be careful.
You'll hurt yourself.

24:11.616 --> 24:13.452
Here, move your feet a little.

24:15.495 --> 24:16.955
You sound like my dad.

24:18.039 --> 24:19.458
Even the way you laugh.

24:19.541 --> 24:20.959
Are you bleeding?

24:22.586 --> 24:23.879
I think it's a cut.

24:23.962 --> 24:26.381
I… I should apply pressure.

24:27.757 --> 24:29.801
It's fine. It's fine.

24:33.555 --> 24:34.389
Just in case.

24:45.150 --> 24:46.568
How is this happening?

24:47.277 --> 24:50.697
I think… I think I'm having
a heart attack.

24:56.661 --> 24:57.787
"Heart attack"?

25:11.259 --> 25:12.260
Every time

25:12.886 --> 25:15.514
I carried those books for you back then,

25:16.431 --> 25:18.225
I would always think,

25:19.267 --> 25:21.603
"I wanna hold her hand.
I wanna hold her hand."

25:23.688 --> 25:25.690
The truth was, by then…

25:25.774 --> 25:26.691
Remember how

25:27.859 --> 25:29.194
I used to say,

25:29.277 --> 25:32.489
"We all have some wickedness
within ourselves?

25:32.572 --> 25:34.699
…we were no longer innocent.

25:35.700 --> 25:37.452
I think I'm rotten on the inside.

25:45.710 --> 25:47.963
We dated
like we were grown-ups.

25:51.716 --> 25:54.719
It wasn't puppy love.
We knew what we wanted.

26:20.328 --> 26:21.997
Quit it. You look crazy.

26:23.248 --> 26:26.251
What's with the face,
and what are you doing with your hands?

26:27.168 --> 26:31.047
Knock it off.
That face makes you look like a fool.

26:31.131 --> 26:34.718
Hey, come on. Can't you draw me like
the girl in Titanic?

26:35.927 --> 26:39.472
Oh no. I can't draw you like Jack drew.

26:39.556 --> 26:42.434
The model he used was different,
and so was the situation.

26:42.517 --> 26:43.852
"The situation"?

26:46.313 --> 26:47.772
What can we do about that?

26:47.856 --> 26:49.065
Wow.

26:49.149 --> 26:51.192
-Why, Mr. Park Toto…
-Park Toto.

26:51.276 --> 26:52.777
Please explain the situation, okay?

26:54.029 --> 26:56.197
You're a naughty boy,
Park Toto, aren't you?

27:01.077 --> 27:02.454
Ugh! Really?

27:03.788 --> 27:06.791
You're not supposed to spit in my face
when you go in for the kiss.

27:06.875 --> 27:09.085
-Come on.
-Stop calling me Park Toto.

27:09.169 --> 27:11.880
-What is so funny to you about that name?
-Stop it.

27:11.963 --> 27:14.215
You used to never laugh
at anything, remember?

27:14.299 --> 27:16.259
Toto and I
had the same sense of humor.

27:16.343 --> 27:17.594
You've been rubbing off on me.

27:17.677 --> 27:19.429
-I'm starting to talk like you.
-Yeah, right.

27:19.512 --> 27:21.306
We had finally cracked the secret

27:21.389 --> 27:24.517
to pretending to be grown-ups,
and we couldn't stop laughing.

27:24.601 --> 27:27.103
It's your fault for making me laugh
when we're kissing.

27:27.187 --> 27:29.105
How am I supposed to concentrate?

27:29.189 --> 27:32.609
Sorry, babe, it's just harder
for me to laugh every day.

27:32.692 --> 27:35.612
That's precious time
we could be using for kissing, right?

27:35.695 --> 27:37.489
That's why we're such a good fit.

27:37.572 --> 27:39.741
-It doesn't need garlic.
-Okay.

27:41.701 --> 27:44.663
I've been noticing
you really like raw fish.

27:44.746 --> 27:46.039
You're always eating it.

27:46.665 --> 27:47.707
I like it.

27:51.127 --> 27:53.713
Listen, how would you like to…

27:55.090 --> 27:56.549
to eat some real amberjack?

27:57.842 --> 27:59.511
-Real amberjack?
-Mm-hmm.

28:00.095 --> 28:01.638
Real amberjack.

28:04.808 --> 28:06.059
At last…

28:11.398 --> 28:14.818
The two men in my life
finally met each other.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.447
Jeez.

28:20.615 --> 28:22.617
Amberjack, my foot.

28:23.201 --> 28:24.911
We're getting nothing but sauries.

28:32.419 --> 28:35.880
Dad, stop!
Why are you looking at him like that?

28:36.548 --> 28:39.008
Can't you see how uncomfortable
you're making him feel?

28:39.634 --> 28:43.638
The day had come
when I had to choose my man over my dad.

28:45.598 --> 28:47.350
This is just how I look.

28:47.934 --> 28:51.020
Then can you please go
a little easier on him?

28:51.104 --> 28:53.815
The open sea is a tough place
for people from the mainland.

28:53.898 --> 28:55.692
Were you comfortable out here right away?

28:55.775 --> 28:57.736
-I was.
-Yeah, right.

28:59.404 --> 29:02.615
Are you throwing the small ones
back in the water?

29:02.699 --> 29:04.242
You're a kind fisherman, sir.

29:04.951 --> 29:07.829
You really are a……kind man.

29:08.830 --> 29:09.706
It's bait.

29:10.290 --> 29:12.167
We're throwing them out to die.

29:14.002 --> 29:15.378
That's not so nice, isn't it?

29:16.254 --> 29:18.923
Stop glaring at him
and catch me something.

29:19.007 --> 29:20.967
I brought him here
to taste real amberjack,

29:21.050 --> 29:22.927
and I don't wanna disappoint him.

29:37.859 --> 29:38.818
Ooh.

29:39.527 --> 29:43.072
Why are you following her? You creep.
She's only using the bathroom back there.

29:43.865 --> 29:45.158
Sit down and eat some amberjack.

29:45.241 --> 29:47.911
You better enjoy it.
You'll pay full price.

29:48.953 --> 29:49.996
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

29:50.079 --> 29:51.956
Rice cake for sale!

29:54.626 --> 29:56.503
Rice cake for sale!

29:56.586 --> 29:59.297
IMF CRISIS, HALF PRICE FOR JEJU CITIZENS
LET'S EAT AND SURVIVE TOGETHER

29:59.380 --> 30:00.924
Rice cake for sale!

30:01.007 --> 30:04.844
That looks heavy. Won't somebody
buy a rice cake from that woman?

30:06.596 --> 30:08.723
Rice cake for sale!

30:08.807 --> 30:11.643
GATHER THE GOLD IN OUR CLOSETS
TO REVIVE THE NATION'S ECONOMY

30:13.728 --> 30:15.730
Rice cake for sale!

30:15.814 --> 30:16.898
What do you think?

30:16.981 --> 30:20.109
Do you think either of them
will say anything first or not?

30:40.338 --> 30:43.716
But why aren't you over there with them?
Don't you wanna be a part of it?

30:43.800 --> 30:45.093
Maybe she doesn't like him.

30:46.302 --> 30:48.930
You don't like him?
What don't you like about him?

30:50.390 --> 30:51.683
It's not me.

30:57.105 --> 30:59.899
Get off my shoulder now. Cut it out.

31:01.150 --> 31:03.736
Why are you here?
Why did you come to Jeju Island?

31:03.820 --> 31:06.573
Is this a police interrogation?

31:06.656 --> 31:08.825
Stop being so cruel, Dad.

31:10.201 --> 31:12.579
You can't talk, ride boats, or even drink.

31:12.662 --> 31:14.664
What can you do? Tell me!

31:14.747 --> 31:16.583
What can you do for my daughter?

31:17.083 --> 31:19.294
Just watching you sit there
makes me upset.

31:19.377 --> 31:22.088
You come all the way down here,
and you can't even try.

31:23.131 --> 31:23.965
Well,

31:24.591 --> 31:26.050
even if I tried,

31:26.551 --> 31:29.387
if you decide you don't like me, then

31:30.889 --> 31:32.724
no matter what I do, it won't--

31:32.807 --> 31:35.435
So you decided we won't like you,
now you won't even try?

31:35.518 --> 31:36.811
Where'd you find this guy?

31:36.895 --> 31:38.855
Shut up, you little brat.

31:39.439 --> 31:40.273
Let go.

31:40.815 --> 31:42.150
Three, two, one…

31:42.233 --> 31:44.319
Zero. Now what are you gonna do?

31:44.402 --> 31:46.571
Let me go.

31:59.083 --> 32:00.627
What do you think of him, really?

32:01.461 --> 32:02.629
Well, you know,

32:03.880 --> 32:04.923
he's very nice.

32:05.590 --> 32:07.675
I know
you have something to say.

32:07.759 --> 32:09.761
Go ahead and just spit it out.

32:10.762 --> 32:12.555
Here's the thing.

32:13.598 --> 32:14.599
It's his family.

32:17.560 --> 32:18.811
It's who they are.

32:20.146 --> 32:21.314
Oh.

32:24.484 --> 32:25.693
You know,

32:26.361 --> 32:29.197
I am trying to impress you
if you didn't know it.

32:29.280 --> 32:30.448
By doing what?

32:31.032 --> 32:33.242
I haven't detected any effort whatsoever.

32:35.286 --> 32:37.664
For one, I don't eat much.

32:37.747 --> 32:38.831
But today--

32:38.915 --> 32:41.084
How terrible of us
to fill the table with food.

32:42.168 --> 32:43.753
Shut your hole.

32:43.836 --> 32:45.797
I really wanna beat you up right now!

32:45.880 --> 32:47.590
Yeah? Do your worst.

32:48.174 --> 32:49.676
Hmm. You got nothing.

33:00.395 --> 33:01.980
Where do you think you're going?

33:02.063 --> 33:05.066
Why do you keep following her to
the bathroom? What are you planning to do?

33:06.192 --> 33:08.903
It might be dark out there,
but don't you dare.

33:08.987 --> 33:11.155
Well, it's because it's dark tonight.

33:11.239 --> 33:13.783
Hold it. A-ten-hut!

33:13.866 --> 33:15.493
It's dark out there, and…

33:17.954 --> 33:18.913
it's cold.

33:25.753 --> 33:27.714
What is the matter with that guy?

33:27.797 --> 33:30.008
Geum-myeong likes him
more than he likes her.

33:31.801 --> 33:32.844
Don't you see it?

33:32.927 --> 33:35.430
-That punk is making a fool out of--
-Hey.

33:35.513 --> 33:36.597
Respect your brother-in-law.

33:36.681 --> 33:38.683
My what? So you like him?

33:38.766 --> 33:40.143
Stop hoarding the fish.

33:40.226 --> 33:42.645
Don't eat all the good shrimp.
Peel some for him.

33:43.229 --> 33:45.106
Seriously? You like him?

33:45.690 --> 33:46.899
I don't believe this!

33:47.400 --> 33:48.234
Why?

33:56.743 --> 33:59.579
Why do you keep following her?
She's just going to the bathroom.

34:00.163 --> 34:01.664
Just sit down and eat some amberjack,

34:01.748 --> 34:04.333
and you'll pay full price
for what you eat.

34:05.043 --> 34:06.919
Sit your ass down, cadet!

34:08.588 --> 34:09.881
In case she falls.

34:10.590 --> 34:12.592
In case Geum-myeong falls.

34:12.675 --> 34:16.262
What? You think I'd let my daughter
fall in the water, really?

34:16.888 --> 34:18.056
Speak for yourself.

34:18.556 --> 34:19.390
Ten-hut!

34:20.641 --> 34:21.726
A-ten-hut!

34:23.936 --> 34:25.980
I just want to make sure.

34:28.066 --> 34:29.317
I wanna make sure.

34:41.746 --> 34:42.997
I can't win.

34:44.624 --> 34:46.542
How am I supposed to impress your dad?

35:02.058 --> 35:03.059
Oh.

35:08.773 --> 35:09.774
You know what, babe?

35:12.235 --> 35:14.487
You could've tried harder.

35:14.987 --> 35:16.239
I know.

35:17.824 --> 35:19.659
I wanna impress your dad,

35:20.243 --> 35:23.204
but this is just… just how I am, I guess.

35:23.287 --> 35:25.957
Oh. That's how you are?

35:26.541 --> 35:27.750
Sure.

35:27.834 --> 35:30.169
I don't know what I'm supposed to do.

35:30.837 --> 35:33.589
-Uh-huh.
-I've never done any of this before, so--

35:33.673 --> 35:36.342
So what? You think just because

35:36.425 --> 35:40.721
I go up to your mother
and use my highest voice to say "hi,"

35:40.805 --> 35:42.598
that's my personality?

35:44.475 --> 35:46.727
Let me make one thing very clear.

35:46.811 --> 35:48.855
-I am… are you listening, babe?
-Yeah.

35:48.938 --> 35:50.815
I am my father's daughter.

35:50.898 --> 35:54.402
If my dad says no, then we're done.

35:56.154 --> 35:57.280
No wedding.

35:57.363 --> 35:59.282
Babe. Wait.

36:04.620 --> 36:06.372
Tell me why
you're okay with him.

36:08.166 --> 36:10.835
You didn't approve of my wife
right away like this.

36:10.918 --> 36:13.921
I won't sit here and let you
treat her with a double standard.

36:14.005 --> 36:15.715
Go away. Go.

36:15.798 --> 36:19.510
Hey, does your wife know
you pooped your pants in kindergarten?

36:19.594 --> 36:21.470
Does your boyfriend know you use my razor?

36:23.181 --> 36:24.724
Hey. Let me go.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.225
Father.

36:32.982 --> 36:34.108
Oh my.

36:35.484 --> 36:36.652
Father.

36:37.445 --> 36:38.696
Father.

36:39.989 --> 36:42.783
Can I… perhaps, if you'd like,

36:42.867 --> 36:44.785
I can peel those shrimps for you?

36:45.620 --> 36:46.913
Peel them for yourself.

36:47.872 --> 36:49.540
He's a lousy drunk.

36:55.838 --> 36:57.757
Oh, just look at him.

36:57.840 --> 37:00.468
He absolutely adores Geum-myeong.

37:02.220 --> 37:05.723
The best part is
his mom really likes Geum-myeong too.

37:05.806 --> 37:08.726
She says she really adores my daughter.

37:08.809 --> 37:10.478
Isn't that something?

37:11.062 --> 37:13.064
Yeah, yeah,
it's something since it's not nothing.

37:13.147 --> 37:14.690
You cried, didn't you?

37:15.191 --> 37:16.192
Why would I?

37:17.235 --> 37:19.779
Everyone loves Geum-myeong for who she is.

37:19.862 --> 37:20.947
We all know she cried.

37:21.030 --> 37:23.699
Is this really wild honey
from Hallasan Mountain?

37:23.783 --> 37:26.911
We know you are trying
to gift this honey to his mom.

37:26.994 --> 37:31.249
Well, I mean… his mother gave me a gift.

37:31.332 --> 37:33.542
She practically bribed me to like him.

37:34.585 --> 37:36.879
Of course I have to return the favor.

37:37.505 --> 37:39.215
She is just so sweet.

37:40.841 --> 37:43.135
Do you wanna know what his mother gave me?

37:44.053 --> 37:47.598
What is this, some kind of treasure?

37:49.433 --> 37:50.851
It's wrapped so tight.

37:50.935 --> 37:52.520
Why does he have to stay here with us?

37:52.603 --> 37:54.522
Why couldn't he have gotten a hotel?

37:55.231 --> 37:57.483
We can't tell him to sleep at a hotel.

37:57.984 --> 38:00.695
I feel bad enough
that he has to sleep in the living room.

38:00.778 --> 38:02.989
Park Chung-seob is spending
the night under my roof,

38:03.072 --> 38:04.573
and I am not having it, okay?

38:04.657 --> 38:07.159
-I think you're overreacting.
-No way. No way.

38:08.160 --> 38:11.539
Hey, stop going out there.

38:11.622 --> 38:14.458
He won't sneak into her room.
He would never dare.

38:14.542 --> 38:16.711
You've been glaring at him all night.

38:17.628 --> 38:18.546
Hey!

38:18.629 --> 38:20.423
Let me go. Stop.

38:20.506 --> 38:22.466
Sit down. Sit down!

38:22.967 --> 38:24.302
Come on.

38:47.408 --> 38:51.579
Oh, Father. Why do you keep
coming in and out? You should sleep.

38:51.662 --> 38:53.331
And you? Why aren't you sleeping?

38:53.873 --> 38:56.000
Why? You're wide awake.

38:56.083 --> 38:57.209
What are you plotting?

38:58.085 --> 39:01.422
What? What's wrong? What… What?
Is there a problem? What's up?

39:14.143 --> 39:15.186
This past fall,

39:15.269 --> 39:18.731
I went to see my family
and took care of their persimmon trees.

39:19.315 --> 39:22.443
I picked the best ones
and made you these treats.

39:23.277 --> 39:25.071
I tried to put as much care
into making them

39:25.154 --> 39:27.490
as you did when
you were raising Geum-myeong.

39:28.657 --> 39:32.536
I adore your daughter more than I can say.

39:33.454 --> 39:35.414
It was a special gift.

39:35.998 --> 39:39.126
My mom had waited a long time
to hear those words.

39:42.338 --> 39:43.881
Are you standing watch all night?

39:44.882 --> 39:47.510
What are you going to do
if he goes into Geum-myeong's room?

39:49.762 --> 39:51.597
I'll kill him.

39:53.641 --> 39:55.518
I'm afraid there's nothing we can do.

39:55.601 --> 39:58.604
There's no stopping Geum-myeong.
You should know that by now.

39:59.647 --> 40:01.607
Sh, sh, sh, sh.

40:03.234 --> 40:04.735
If you really love her,

40:06.529 --> 40:08.239
it's time to let her go.

40:11.992 --> 40:13.160
Mom knew.

40:17.665 --> 40:20.501
She knew this would happen eventually.

40:21.502 --> 40:25.089
It's the single Bungle Show.
I'm your host Kang Seok.

40:25.172 --> 40:27.591
Many sad expressions
have come out of this crisis.

40:27.675 --> 40:30.845
"Jobless Twenties" because half of
everyone in their twenties is unemployed.

40:30.928 --> 40:33.889
"Thirty-eight and Retired" for those
who had to quit in their late thirties.

40:33.973 --> 40:37.226
"Retirement at 45"
because you couldn't get a job past 45.

40:37.309 --> 40:40.104
And you're called "Job Hogger"
for working past 56.

40:40.187 --> 40:42.440
What a depressing world we live in.

40:42.523 --> 40:45.276
Well, let's listen to
an uplifting song, shall we?

40:50.906 --> 40:53.159
And that's how
I left the nest for good.

41:03.961 --> 41:07.923
Like a little bluebird
soaring high above a bare mountain,

41:09.842 --> 41:12.219
I was nervous but brave.

41:12.303 --> 41:14.346
Don't smile too much today.

41:14.847 --> 41:15.973
You'll annoy your dad.

41:17.933 --> 41:21.604
Mom, don't do that.
Let's all get along. Okay?

41:24.148 --> 41:27.234
Hey, it's not like
you're done with me after today.

41:27.318 --> 41:28.903
You'll still be my mom.

41:28.986 --> 41:30.404
And I'm still me.

41:30.488 --> 41:33.657
My name won't be Park Geum-myeong.
It'll be Yang Geum-myeong.

41:33.741 --> 41:34.909
You know my pager number.

41:34.992 --> 41:36.994
The last four digits are
the same as our home number.

41:37.077 --> 41:38.454
They're not Chung-seob's.

41:39.288 --> 41:41.790
I'm still your daughter.

41:42.416 --> 41:44.877
I know that. You're still our daughter.

41:45.586 --> 41:47.421
So don't cry.

41:48.047 --> 41:49.507
If you cry, so will I.

41:49.590 --> 41:51.342
You'll ruin the wedding photos.

41:55.012 --> 41:57.014
Let's keep it nice and cool today.

41:58.057 --> 41:59.808
How's that sound? Hmm?

42:43.602 --> 42:45.104
Hello!

42:45.187 --> 42:47.231
I can't believe you came.

42:47.314 --> 42:49.525
We're invited, so why would we not come?

42:49.608 --> 42:51.777
Now, the girl who's getting married…

42:51.860 --> 42:54.822
Is she the same little girl
who loved caramel?

42:54.905 --> 42:57.283
Yes, you always gave her free candy.

42:57.366 --> 42:58.284
It's Geum-myeong.

42:58.367 --> 42:59.827
Mm.

43:00.411 --> 43:02.204
-Go on in. Please.
-Go ahead, please.

43:02.288 --> 43:04.248
-It's wrinkled.
-Yeah, it is.

43:04.331 --> 43:05.416
They got you.

43:05.499 --> 43:07.418
Oh, aren't you done up?

43:10.671 --> 43:12.381
-Where's Ju-gyeong?
-Ju-gyeong?

43:12.464 --> 43:14.550
Wow, the photographer's late?

43:14.633 --> 43:15.593
She's right there.

43:16.343 --> 43:17.720
-Hey!
-Hey!

43:30.357 --> 43:31.567
I shouldn't have come.

43:32.526 --> 43:34.987
-Ju-gyeong!
-Hey! Hey!

43:35.070 --> 43:36.572
Hurry up. Hurry, hurry!

43:36.655 --> 43:38.824
Hey! Let's get set up.

43:44.330 --> 43:47.041
-Oh my God, they burst!
-She's so damn beautiful.

43:48.042 --> 43:50.336
Hey, what kind of photographer is late?

43:50.419 --> 43:52.338
-You missed me getting out of the car.
-Uh-huh.

43:52.421 --> 43:55.382
-Wow! Aren't we confident today?
-Mm-hmm.

43:58.344 --> 43:59.178
Okay.

43:59.261 --> 44:00.929
Take pictures of me from here.

44:01.013 --> 44:01.889
Okay.

44:03.766 --> 44:05.559
Look at you.

44:05.643 --> 44:06.685
So pretty today.

44:06.769 --> 44:08.437
-Here. On those steps.
-Let's get one there.

44:08.520 --> 44:10.856
In the end,
not everyone gets married

44:10.939 --> 44:13.275
to their first or most passionate love.

44:14.318 --> 44:17.529
Not that I loved him less,
but the temperature was different.

44:17.613 --> 44:20.240
Oh, you sent us so many lovely tangerines.

44:20.324 --> 44:22.493
You never have to buy
another tangerine again.

44:22.576 --> 44:26.121
It was just
the right temperature for me to be myself.

44:26.205 --> 44:28.624
-Oh my.
-Have you said hello?

44:28.707 --> 44:32.711
At last,
I had finally found my prince.

44:52.189 --> 44:53.857
It's a match made in heaven.

44:53.941 --> 44:56.110
Was he always that silly,
or did you teach him?

44:56.193 --> 44:57.736
Yes, I did.

44:59.113 --> 45:00.239
Oh, how gorgeous.

45:05.494 --> 45:07.496
The groom will now enter.

45:09.415 --> 45:11.875
Here comes our brave groom
down the aisle.

45:11.959 --> 45:14.294
Let's all welcome him
with a round of applause.

45:26.306 --> 45:29.309
Didn't I tell everyone I hate it
when people cry at weddings?

45:30.561 --> 45:34.022
Just don't cry, Dad.
If you do, I'm gonna be so mad.

45:34.106 --> 45:35.983
Uh… uh, you know,

45:36.066 --> 45:38.986
it's better if you just
don't look at me for the entire time.

45:42.448 --> 45:43.449
Geum-myeong.

45:45.617 --> 45:46.994
You sure you want this?

45:47.828 --> 45:48.787
Because if you don't,

45:49.371 --> 45:52.082
you can just back out
and run right back to me, all right?

46:00.257 --> 46:01.884
Are you sure you want to eat this?

46:02.384 --> 46:04.344
If it tastes bad, just back out.

46:04.845 --> 46:06.180
Just spit it out, okay?

46:11.685 --> 46:12.686
There we go.

46:14.146 --> 46:15.147
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

46:16.523 --> 46:17.566
Do these fit?

46:25.240 --> 46:27.701
Make sure to say "Hello" like this
when you meet your teacher.

46:27.785 --> 46:29.828
Just like this? "Hello, teacher."

46:29.912 --> 46:30.746
Oh.

46:33.665 --> 46:36.293
Honey, we can't send her
to school like this.

46:36.919 --> 46:38.420
Let's wait until next year.

46:38.504 --> 46:41.840
Oh my, oh my. Don't keep her here forever,
all right, Gwan Sik?

46:42.883 --> 46:44.676
What are you gonna do
when she gets married?

46:44.760 --> 46:46.178
You're being silly. Daddy's silly.

46:46.261 --> 46:48.722
Geum-myeong, are you sure you're ready?

46:49.348 --> 46:52.142
I'm sure, Dad. Jeong-geun is going.

46:52.226 --> 46:54.186
What Jeong-geun does
is not your concern, okay?

46:54.269 --> 46:56.563
I'm not sure I like it
that you two are so close.

46:56.647 --> 46:58.023
I want to go to school.

47:00.901 --> 47:03.070
Fine, go to school for now.

47:03.153 --> 47:05.280
If you don't like it, back out.
Understand?

47:05.364 --> 47:07.032
Just run back home to me, all right?

47:07.616 --> 47:09.243
I'll be here, waiting for you. Hmm?

47:09.326 --> 47:10.160
Mm-hmm!

47:13.163 --> 47:13.997
Oh my.

47:14.915 --> 47:18.252
Geum-myeong, you think you'll be able
to run fast in these?

47:18.752 --> 47:21.171
-I think I'll be in first place, Dad.
-First?

47:21.255 --> 47:22.297
-Ready, whoa!
-Go!

47:22.381 --> 47:24.633
You have to wait
until I say go, all right?

47:25.342 --> 47:27.386
Listen. You don't have to win Geum-myeong.

47:27.469 --> 47:29.221
If you don't wanna do it, back out.

47:29.304 --> 47:31.014
And if you happen to fall
out there tomorrow,

47:31.098 --> 47:33.392
Dad will be right behind you. Got it?

47:33.475 --> 47:34.393
Mm!

47:34.476 --> 47:36.019
-Ready? Go!
-Go!

47:37.688 --> 47:39.314
Oh gosh, no.

47:39.398 --> 47:40.941
YOU CAN EASILY SCORE HIGH!

47:44.194 --> 47:46.196
COLLEGE ENTRANCE EXAM IDENTIFICATION SLIP

47:46.280 --> 47:47.656
Good luck!

47:48.657 --> 47:50.367
Good luck, everyone!

47:50.868 --> 47:52.536
Let's go, Munil High!

47:53.453 --> 47:56.164
-We always show up way too early.
-Let's go!

47:56.248 --> 47:59.918
Oh my God. Why is everyone
in this family so diligent?

48:00.002 --> 48:02.963
What did you go through in life
that's made you like this?

48:04.006 --> 48:06.174
Geum-myeong,
you're good at guessing answers, right?

48:07.593 --> 48:09.469
Why would I guess the answers?

48:09.553 --> 48:11.763
Dad, I'm Yang Geum-myeong.

48:12.890 --> 48:13.932
You're right.

48:14.016 --> 48:16.602
I've been watching you all these years,
and I know you'll do well.

48:16.685 --> 48:19.479
You're so good at everything
that I just know you will.

48:19.563 --> 48:21.565
Is that all you have to say to me
right now, Dad?

48:22.149 --> 48:24.234
Aren't you gonna tell me
to back out if I want?

48:24.318 --> 48:26.945
Well, yes, of course.
If your head hurts, and you can't do it,

48:27.821 --> 48:28.864
just back out.

48:28.947 --> 48:31.658
Just run away,
and I'll be here waiting for you, okay?

48:32.284 --> 48:34.620
When I back out, you always have my back.

48:36.455 --> 48:39.333
Almost time.
Are you sure you don't want any tea?

48:44.755 --> 48:45.672
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

48:45.756 --> 48:47.674
THE PRIDE OF DODONG!
MY DAUGHTER WILL GET IN!

48:48.300 --> 48:51.178
Every time
I had to walk a tightrope,

48:51.261 --> 48:54.181
my dad was always holding a net close by.

48:55.807 --> 48:57.726
"I'll catch you if you fall,"
he would say.

48:58.977 --> 49:01.396
I should've told him when I had the chance

49:03.148 --> 49:05.525
just how comforting his words were to me.

49:06.026 --> 49:07.611
At least once.

49:08.320 --> 49:11.156
It must've snowed
the whole time he was standing there,

49:11.823 --> 49:14.576
waiting for his daughter
to come back to him.

49:18.246 --> 49:20.999
The bride will now enter
to walk down the aisle.

49:21.667 --> 49:22.751
Geum-myeong.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.712
Your dad's right here.

49:25.796 --> 49:27.172
You know that.

49:27.255 --> 49:29.800
Go ahead. Do whatever you want, dear.
It's your call, okay?

49:31.385 --> 49:33.720
In the midst of
my dad's wintertime,

49:33.804 --> 49:35.973
I began a new chapter in my life.

49:36.056 --> 49:38.225
They had spent their youth
watching me grow

49:38.725 --> 49:40.727
until I became my own person.

49:45.941 --> 49:48.276
If Chung-seob makes you mad,
you can back out.

49:48.360 --> 49:49.736
Dad's always here for you, okay?

49:50.404 --> 49:51.363
Stop it.

49:51.989 --> 49:55.575
Why would you start
saying things like that right now, huh?

49:56.159 --> 49:58.328
God, you're so frustrating.

49:59.788 --> 50:00.789
And now,

50:01.665 --> 50:02.541
the bride!

50:07.129 --> 50:09.256
Put your hands together
for the bride.

50:34.114 --> 50:36.450
Gwang-rye must be smiling ear to ear.

50:36.533 --> 50:37.492
I'm sure of it!

50:38.577 --> 50:40.203
She must be so happy.

50:43.248 --> 50:44.583
At Ae-sun's wedding,

50:45.083 --> 50:49.504
I was the one who couldn't stop crying
when her uncle walked her down the aisle.

50:49.588 --> 50:53.592
Mom kept smiling
because seeing her daughter's blessings

50:53.675 --> 50:55.343
was like winning a medal to her.

50:58.305 --> 51:00.557
Uh, the groom is now approaching
the weeping bride

51:00.640 --> 51:02.976
in the hopes of convincing her
to walk forward.

51:03.643 --> 51:05.812
Please give them another hand
to encourage them.

51:10.192 --> 51:11.234
Geum-myeong.

51:13.320 --> 51:14.863
You said we'd keep it cool.

51:15.572 --> 51:16.698
You're bawling your eyes out.

51:24.998 --> 51:26.041
Are we not getting married?

51:27.292 --> 51:28.210
Should we stop?

51:30.837 --> 51:32.130
Let's do it.

51:35.842 --> 51:36.676
Here.

51:58.490 --> 52:00.450
The day before Dad passed,

52:01.493 --> 52:04.579
I told him, "Dad, I'm sorry. I'm sorry."

52:05.997 --> 52:08.500
I must have said it a hundred times over.

52:09.918 --> 52:11.461
That's when Dad told me,

52:12.546 --> 52:14.923
"There's nothing to be sorry about."

52:15.006 --> 52:18.552
"From the day you were born,
I was already in heaven."

52:29.688 --> 52:33.692
See? Didn't I say your dad would cry
more than your mom?

52:35.610 --> 52:37.654
My dad's crying?

52:52.419 --> 52:54.713
I didn't think your dad
would drink like that.

52:55.547 --> 52:58.466
Why are men always so tough
on their son-in-laws?

52:59.050 --> 53:01.094
We all know he can't hold his liquor.

53:01.178 --> 53:03.763
He wanted to see
what kind of drunk Chung-seob was.

53:03.847 --> 53:06.683
Instead,
we get to see what kind of a drunk he is.

53:07.350 --> 53:09.227
-Oh.
-Hey, Dad.

53:09.311 --> 53:10.145
Hey.

53:15.859 --> 53:17.110
What about your mom?

53:18.195 --> 53:19.029
Sir?

53:19.112 --> 53:20.906
Does she like Geum-myeong or not?

53:21.698 --> 53:22.532
Oh.

53:23.116 --> 53:26.661
My mother always goes on and on
about wanting a daughter of her own.

53:27.579 --> 53:29.789
Honestly, I think
she likes her better than me, so--

53:29.873 --> 53:30.832
Not that.

53:32.167 --> 53:34.878
-Sorry?
-Not as a daughter-in-law. Not that.

53:35.754 --> 53:37.631
Does she like her as a daughter of mine!

53:38.131 --> 53:40.634
Oh, right. Yes.

53:40.717 --> 53:43.261
-Park Chung-seob!
-Yes, Father.

53:43.345 --> 53:46.640
Do you have any idea
whom you're taking from me?

53:47.432 --> 53:48.600
Sir?

53:49.476 --> 53:51.186
I am giving you…

53:53.813 --> 53:56.149
my heaven on earth…

53:58.276 --> 54:00.695
…even though you've done
absolutely nothing for her

54:01.446 --> 54:03.698
throughout the first 30 years of her life.

54:05.867 --> 54:07.202
From what I heard,

54:07.285 --> 54:10.664
Mrs. Oh was the bookworm
that had a way with words.

54:15.794 --> 54:16.962
Hey, "Heaven on Earth."

54:17.504 --> 54:18.588
Carry your own honey.

54:21.800 --> 54:26.054
That's how my dad
was forever robbed of his unrequited love.

54:26.846 --> 54:30.350
Now, the bride and the groom
will face the bride's parents.

54:38.650 --> 54:42.195
The bride and the groom
will bow to the bride's parents.

54:54.416 --> 54:55.250
What?

54:55.750 --> 54:57.961
The bride's father is crying. He's crying.

54:58.044 --> 54:59.504
Be quiet. Be quiet.

54:59.587 --> 55:02.549
The bride's father
must've truly adored his daughter.

55:02.632 --> 55:04.009
Of course he's crying.

55:04.092 --> 55:07.429
Gwan-sik is being robbed of his treasure
in front of everyone.

55:07.512 --> 55:10.515
He wouldn't cry like that
if I ever got remarried.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.980
I wish you both all the best. Go.

55:18.648 --> 55:21.651
Next, the bride and the groom
will bow to the groom's mother.

55:22.152 --> 55:25.280
Pull yourself together, will you?

55:27.407 --> 55:29.451
God, you're so embarrassing.

55:30.201 --> 55:33.788
The bride and the groom
will bow to his mother.

55:48.219 --> 55:50.889
Who is it? Who's paging at this hour?

55:50.972 --> 55:52.932
Who is this?

55:53.558 --> 55:54.809
I don't know who this is.

55:56.144 --> 55:58.980
I thought I told you
to dye your hair for the wedding.

55:59.064 --> 56:00.690
It's turning gray.

56:01.649 --> 56:03.860
Geum-myeong is going to
nag at me about that.

56:04.444 --> 56:06.488
Oh, that girl.

56:07.238 --> 56:10.450
I took good care of my husband.
She didn't look after her father.

56:10.533 --> 56:13.453
From now on,
she can take care of her own husband.

56:18.416 --> 56:22.045
Life never allows us
to relish these moments for too long.

56:23.963 --> 56:25.090
Yang Eun-myeong.

56:31.137 --> 56:31.971
And you are?

56:32.972 --> 56:37.018
Happiness arrives before us,
but trouble approaches from behind.

56:37.519 --> 56:39.020
Park Cheol-yong, your partner.

56:39.687 --> 56:40.522
Where is he?

56:42.607 --> 56:43.441
What?

56:47.112 --> 56:49.781
When your mom tells you
not to hang out with a friend,

56:51.199 --> 56:52.951
she has a good reason.

59:38.032 --> 59:43.329
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."
